A Maven plugin is just a JAR with a **Mojo** (goal) class. Below is a minimal custom plugin that iterates through **all system environment variables** (`System.getenv()`), with an option to filter by prefix and to optionally write them to a file.

## 1) Plugin `pom.xml`

```xml
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <groupId>com.example</groupId>
  <artifactId>env-dump-maven-plugin</artifactId>
  <version>1.0.0</version>
  <packaging>maven-plugin</packaging>

  <properties>
    <maven.plugin.api.version>3.9.6</maven.plugin.api.version>
    <maven.plugin.tools.version>3.10.2</maven.plugin.tools.version>
    <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
    <maven.compiler.release>17</maven.compiler.release>
  </properties>

  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.maven</groupId>
      <artifactId>maven-plugin-api</artifactId>
      <version>${maven.plugin.api.version}</version>
      <scope>provided</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugin-tools</groupId>
      <artifactId>maven-plugin-annotations</artifactId>
      <version>${maven.plugin.tools.version}</version>
      <scope>provided</scope>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-plugin-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${maven.plugin.tools.version}</version>
        <executions>
          <execution>
            <id>default-descriptor</id>
            <goals>
              <goal>descriptor</goal>
            </goals>
          </execution>
        </executions>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
```

## 2) Mojo class (goal)

Create `src/main/java/com/example/maven/EnvDumpMojo.java`:

```java
package com.example.maven;

import org.apache.maven.plugin.AbstractMojo;
import org.apache.maven.plugin.MojoExecutionException;
import org.apache.maven.plugins.annotations.Mojo;
import org.apache.maven.plugins.annotations.Parameter;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.util.Map;

import static java.util.stream.Collectors.joining;

@Mojo(name = "dump-env", threadSafe = true)
public class EnvDumpMojo extends AbstractMojo {

  /**
   * If set, only variables whose names start with this prefix are emitted.
   */
  @Parameter(property = "env.prefix")
  private String prefix;

  /**
   * Optional output file (e.g. ${project.build.directory}/env.txt).
   * If omitted, variables are logged to the Maven console.
   */
  @Parameter(property = "env.outputFile")
  private java.io.File outputFile;

  /**
   * If true, sorts environment variables by name for stable output.
   */
  @Parameter(property = "env.sort", defaultValue = "true")
  private boolean sort;

  @Override
  public void execute() throws MojoExecutionException {
    Map<String, String> env = System.getenv();

    var stream = env.entrySet().stream();
    if (prefix != null && !prefix.isBlank()) {
      stream = stream.filter(e -> e.getKey().startsWith(prefix));
    }
    if (sort) {
      stream = stream.sorted(Map.Entry.comparingByKey());
    }

    String text = stream
        .map(e -> e.getKey() + "=" + e.getValue())
        .collect(joining(System.lineSeparator(), "", System.lineSeparator()));

    if (outputFile == null) {
      getLog().info("Environment variables:");
      // Avoid a single huge line; log line-by-line.
      for (String line : text.split("\\R")) {
        if (!line.isEmpty()) getLog().info(line);
      }
    } else {
      try {
        Files.createDirectories(outputFile.toPath().getParent());
        Files.writeString(outputFile.toPath(), text, StandardCharsets.UTF_8);
        getLog().info("Wrote environment variables to: " + outputFile.getAbsolutePath());
      } catch (IOException e) {
        throw new MojoExecutionException("Failed writing to " + outputFile, e);
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## 3) Build & run it

Build the plugin:

```bash
mvn -q -DskipTests package
```

Install locally (so another project can use it):

```bash
mvn -q -DskipTests install
```

Run the goal directly:

```bash
mvn com.example:env-dump-maven-plugin:1.0.0:dump-env
```

Optional filtering/output:

```bash
mvn com.example:env-dump-maven-plugin:1.0.0:dump-env \
  -Denv.prefix=JAVA \
  -Denv.outputFile=target/env.txt
```

If you tell me your Java/Maven versions and whether you want it bound to a lifecycle phase (e.g., `validate`), I can show the `<plugin>` configuration snippet for a consuming project.
